  "obligation": "Allocate exception tags and link imports/reexports using original heap identity and exact closed declaration equality, in the single shared VM.",
  "representation": "WasmTag owns source type index and optional import name. The validated original declaration graph remains shared. A live WasmTag heap cell owns identity and original graph/type; equal types allocate distinct identities per definition and instantiation. Imported bindings retain the original cell. Mixed declaration lookup order derives from the resource/name projection. Tag slots precede the final imported-function suffix, preserving ref.func base derivation without new offset metadata. Heap tracing/profiling derive a new non-edge-bearing cell kind. No opcode, residual format, payload execution, side registry or second executor is added.",
  "scope": "Eight matching pinned files: tags, imports, linking, exports, globals, starts, indirect calls and exact-function imports. Thirteen focused directives and thirteen Node observations cover shifted foreign types, mixed tag/function/global/memory/table imports, direct/indirect calls, copied identity and rejected links before start effects. Rust internal controls additionally prove distinct same-type identities and root release/retention through GC. No full suites, expectations, skips or inventory changes.",
